{{if .interview_with_docs}}Interview me relentlessly about every aspect of this plan until we reach a shared understanding. Ask the questions one at a time, waiting for feedback on each question before continuing.{{else}}{{if eq .agent "claude-code"}}Interview me using the AskUserQuestionTool relentlessly about every aspect of this plan until we reach a shared understanding.{{else}}Ask the user directly in conversation relentlessly about every aspect of this plan until reaching a shared understanding.{{end}}{{end}} For each question, include your weighted recommendation [strong|neutral|weak]. Walk down each branch of the design tree, resolving dependencies between decisions one-by-one.

If a question can be answered by exploring the codebase, explore the codebase instead.

## Locating the plan

This project's plans dir is `{{.plans_dir}}` (resolved from the current project's plan-bender config — relative paths are relative to the project root, absolute paths are absolute). Resolve the plan strictly from there:

1. If the user named a slug, read `{{.plans_dir}}/<slug>/prd.json` and any files under `{{.plans_dir}}/<slug>/issues/`.
2. If the user did not name a slug, list `{{.plans_dir}}/` and pick the one in-progress plan; if there are zero or multiple, ask which one.
3. If `{{.plans_dir}}/` does not exist or is empty, ASK the user which plan to interview about. Do not infer from earlier conversation snippets, transcripts, or paths from other projects.

Never read a PRD from any path outside `{{.plans_dir}}/`. A plan referenced from another project's transcript is not in scope here — ask, don't fetch.
